# Copy to .env (make quickstart does) and add a key for the assistant. Without one, the
# map, search, weights and profiles all work, and the assistant answers its suggested
# questions from recordings.

# Which model drives the assistant (provider:model). With an OpenRouter key, one key
# reaches many providers. Claude Haiku 5.5 answers in about 4 seconds for about $0.001 a
# question and passes every assistant eval (docs/evals.md); so does the fallback, an
# open-weights model on a different provider.
LIX_MODEL=openrouter:anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5
LIX_FALLBACK_MODELS=openrouter:qwen/qwen3.8-27b
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_APP_TITLE=UK Liveability Index

# Or another provider: anthropic:claude-opus-5-5, openai:gpt-5, google:gemini-2.5-pro,
# ollama:llama3.1 (local; docker compose --profile local-llm). "test" is a scripted
# assistant for tests, "replay" the recorded answers only.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Caps, so a shared key can't run up a bill. A refused question gets a chat reply; the
# map keeps working. Costs count what the provider reports (OpenRouter does). Also set a
# credit limit on the key itself: that is the real backstop.
# LIX_SESSION_TURNS=30       # questions per conversation
# LIX_RATE_PER_MINUTE=20     # questions per minute, everyone together
# LIX_DAILY_BUDGET=1.00      # per UTC day; 0 turns it off
# LIX_REQUEST_LIMIT=8        # model requests per question
# LIX_TOOL_CALL_LIMIT=12     # tool calls per question
# LIX_TOKEN_LIMIT=150000     # tokens per question (what bounds a question's cost)
# LIX_MODEL_TIMEOUT=60       # seconds per model request

# Reasoning effort (low is plenty for picking tools)
# LIX_EFFORT=low

# The port the app is served on (docker compose)
# LIX_PORT=3000

# Keep data on another disk (defaults to ./data)
# LIX_DATA_DIR=/Volumes/data/lix

# Data sources behind a free key (open licences; the build skips them with a warning
# when a key is missing). The key is sent with the request and never written anywhere.
# LOGAINM_API_KEY=            # Irish place names: https://www.gaois.ie/en/technology/developers/
